  "concept": {
    "movement": "A watchful, low mongoose amble with visible thigh motion and full alternating steps. Faster travel becomes a quick diagonal dart with small paw clearance, a quiet back and a trailing centered tail.",
    "attack": "A sharp low dart and head-led nip: load briefly backward, drive the shoulders and muzzle forward over a quick forepaw step, brace, then recover the hind feet and forefeet in sequence.",
